<h1>Anchor AI costs</h1>
<section aria-label="Inference deployment comparison">
  <h2>Which workloads might justify self-hosting?</h2>
  <p>Export this organization's daily workload tokens, accounting costs and available latency aggregates.
    No ticket text, customer identifiers or other organizations' records are included.</p>
  <%= link_to 'Export deployment comparison usage', url_for(organization_id: params[:organization_id], window: @window, comparison: 'export', only_path: true) %>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Workload</th><th>Initial option to evaluate</th><th>Evidence still required</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Bursty ticket triage</td><td>Hosted or managed warm capacity; dedicated local capacity may sit idle.</td><td>Processing approval, equivalent quality, warm/cold latency, peak demand and recovery.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sustained KB embedding</td><td>Self-hosted if demand amortizes the fully loaded fleet.</td><td>Embedding quality, measured throughput, headroom, GPU hours, storage/network and on-call costs.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Run bin/compare_hosted_local.py with the export to produce a workload-specific matrix.
    Unknown workload classes require an operator-reviewed policy. Accounting units are not dollar quotes.
    Missing latency is not zero latency. Fixture comparisons cannot approve production routing.</p>
</section>
<p><%= @window %> — <%= @config.fetch('unit') %></p>
<p>Price: <%= @config.fetch('price_version') %>; budget: <%= @config.fetch('budget_version') %></p>
<% if @config.fetch('fixture') %><p>Illustrative fake-provider accounting; not a dollar invoice.</p><% end %>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Total</th><th>Budget</th><th>Alert</th>
    <% AiBudgetCounter::DRIVERS.each do |driver| %><th><%= driver %></th><% end %>
    <th>Input tokens</th><th>Cached subset</th><th>Output tokens</th><th>Reasoning subset</th>
    <th>Embedding tokens</th><th>Attempts</th><th>Cache savings</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody><% @counters.each do |counter| %>
    <tr><td><%= counter.feature %></td><td><%= counter.total %></td>
      <td><%= @config.fetch('budgets').fetch(counter.feature).fetch('limit') %></td>
      <td><%= counter.warning?(@config) ? 'WARNING' : 'below threshold' %></td>
      <% AiBudgetCounter::DRIVERS.each do |driver| %><td><%= counter[driver] %></td><% end %>
      <% %w[input_tokens cached_tokens output_tokens reasoning_tokens embedding_tokens attempts cache_savings].each do |metric| %>
        <td><%= counter[metric] %></td>
      <% end %>
    </tr>
  <% end %></tbody>
</table>
